IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc22-counts`

-- ccc22-tests-counts.l4 -- tests for ccc22-counts.l4 (sections 581 to 588). Expected values are written from the text, beside the assertion. Arguments are in the order of each function's GIVEN lines.

§ `Section 581`

-- (1): args: a single transaction, a statement in substance that the accused committed an offence therein specified.
#ASSERT `s 581(1) the count is in the form subsection (1) requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(1) the count is in the form subsection (1) requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "shall contain in substance a statement"
#ASSERT `s 581(1) the count is in the form subsection (1) requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "in general" apply to a single transaction
-- (2): arg: the form.
#ASSERT `s 581(2) the statement may be in this form` `s 581(2)(a) popular language without technical averments or allegations of matters that are not essential to be proved` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(2) the statement may be in this form` `s 581(2)(b) the words of the enactment that describes the offence or declares the matters charged to be an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(2) the statement may be in this form` `s 581(2)(c) words that are sufficient to give to the accused notice of the offence with which he is charged` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(2) the statement may be in this form` `s 581(2) some other form` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): args: reasonable information, identifies the transaction.
#ASSERT `s 581(3) the count contains sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(3) the count contains sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 581(3) the count contains sufficient detail of the circumstances of the alleged offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 581(3) the absence or insufficiency of details vitiates the count` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "does not vitiate the count"
#ASSERT `s 581(3) the absence or insufficiency of details vitiates the count` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "but otherwise": the subsection does not say
-- (4): args: the offence charged (section, subsection), every overt act relied on is stated.
#ASSERT `s 581(4) the indictment states every overt act to be relied on` (`Provision of the Code` OF 47, "(1)") TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(4) the indictment states every overt act to be relied on` (`Provision of the Code` OF 50, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- sections 50 to 53: the first
#ASSERT `s 581(4) the indictment states every overt act to be relied on` (`Provision of the Code` OF 53, "") FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- sections 50 to 53: the last
#ASSERT `s 581(4) the indictment states every overt act to be relied on` (`Provision of the Code` OF 54, "") FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- just outside the range
#ASSERT `s 581(4) the indictment states every overt act to be relied on` (`Provision of the Code` OF 49, "") TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- just outside the range
#ASSERT `s 581(4) the indictment states every overt act to be relied on` (`Provision of the Code` OF 48, "") FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- section 48 is not section 47
-- (5): args: the provision is a section, subsection, paragraph or subparagraph of the enactment creating the offence; the count refers to one.
#ASSERT `s 581(5) the count may refer to the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(5) the count may refer to the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 581(5) the reference is considered in determining whether the count is sufficient` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 581(5) the reference is considered in determining whether the count is sufficient` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): arg: the provision relates to matters that do not render a count insufficient.
#ASSERT `s 581(6) the provision restricts or limits the application of section 581` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 581(6) the provision restricts or limits the application of section 581` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 582`

-- args: the offence is high treason or first degree murder, the person is specifically charged with that offence in the indictment.
#ASSERT `s 582 the section bars a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 582 the section bars a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless ... he is specifically charged"
#ASSERT `s 582 the section bars a conviction for high treason or first degree murder` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another offence, such as second degree murder

§ `Section 583`

#ASSERT `s 583 the absence of details renders the count insufficient` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the court's opinion that the count otherwise fulfils section 581
#ASSERT `s 583 the absence of details renders the count insufficient` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(a) it does not name the person injured or intended or attempted to be injured` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(b) it does not name the person who owns or has a special property or interest in property mentioned in the count` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(c) it charges an intent to defraud without naming or describing the person whom it was intended to defraud` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(d) it does not set out any writing that is the subject of the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(e) it does not set out the words used where words that are alleged to have been used are the subject of the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(f) it does not specify the means by which the alleged offence was committed` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(g) it does not name or describe with precision any person, place or thing` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583(h) it does not, where the consent of a person, official or authority is required before proceedings may be instituted for an offence, state that the consent has been obtained` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 583 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 583 some other omission` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "without restricting the generality of the foregoing"

§ `Section 584`

-- (1): args: the count is for a libel or obscene matter, the only omission is the words or writing not being set out.
#ASSERT `s 584(1) the omission alone renders the count insufficient` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 584(1) the omission alone renders the count insufficient` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 584(1) the omission alone renders the count insufficient` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 584(2) the count may charge that the published matter was written in a sense that by innuendo made the publication criminal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 584(2) the count may charge that the published matter was written in a sense that by innuendo made the publication criminal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 584(3) proof that the matter published was libellous is sufficient` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 584(3) proof that the matter published was libellous is sufficient` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 584(3) proof that the matter published was libellous is sufficient` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 585`

-- args: the charge, the omission.
#ASSERT `s 585 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 585(a) perjury` `s 585 it does not state the nature of the authority of the tribunal before which the oath or statement was taken or made` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 585 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 585(b) the making of a false oath or a false statement` `s 585 it does not state the subject of the inquiry` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 585 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 585(c) fabricating evidence` `s 585 it does not state the words used or the evidence fabricated` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 585 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 585(d) procuring the commission of an offence mentioned in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` `s 585 it does not expressly negative the truth of the words used` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 585 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 585 some other charge` `s 585 it does not state the subject of the inquiry` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 585 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` `s 585(a) perjury` `s 585 some other omission` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 586`

#ASSERT `s 586 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 586 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 586 the omission alone renders the count insufficient` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 587`

#ASSERT `s 587(1) the court may order the prosecutor to furnish particulars` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the court may order the prosecutor to furnish particulars` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "where it is satisfied that it is necessary for a fair trial" (ruling (b): where)
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1)(a) of what is relied on in support of a charge of perjury, the making of a false oath or a false statement, fabricating evidence or counselling the commission of any of those offences` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1)(b) of any false pretence or fraud that is alleged` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1)(c) of any alleged attempt or conspiracy by fraudulent means` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1)(d) setting out the passages in a book, pamphlet, newspaper or other printing or writing that are relied on in support of a charge of selling or exhibiting an obscene book` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1)(e) further describing any writing or words that are the subject of a charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1)(f) further describing the means by which an offence is alleged to have been committed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1)(g) further describing a person, place or thing referred to in an indictment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(1) the particulars are of a kind the subsection lists` `s 587(1) some other particulars` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 587(2) the court may give consideration to any evidence that has been taken` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(2) the court may give consideration to any evidence that has been taken` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): args: a particular is delivered, the consequence.
#ASSERT `s 587(3) the consequence follows where a particular is delivered` TRUE `s 587(3)(a) a copy is given without charge to the accused or his counsel` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(3) the consequence follows where a particular is delivered` TRUE `s 587(3)(b) the particular is entered in the record` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(3) the consequence follows where a particular is delivered` TRUE `s 587(3)(c) the trial proceeds in all respects as if the indictment had been amended to conform with the particular` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 587(3) the consequence follows where a particular is delivered` FALSE `s 587(3)(a) a copy is given without charge to the accused or his counsel` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 587(3) the consequence follows where a particular is delivered` TRUE `s 587(3) some other consequence` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 588`

-- args: s 2 property (a MAYBE), the person has by law the management, control or custody, the proceeding is against any other person for an offence on or in respect of the property.
#ASSERT `s 588 the property is deemed to be the property of the person who has the management, control or custody of it` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 588 the property is deemed to be the property of the person who has the management, control or custody of it` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 588 the property is deemed to be the property of the person who has the management, control or custody of it` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 588 the property is deemed to be the property of the person who has the management, control or custody of it` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- whether it is property is for section 2
#ASSERT `s 588 the property is deemed to be the property of the person who has the management, control or custody of it` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
